{
  "schemaVersion": 6,
  "contractId": "timor-leste-honorary-consulate-content.v1",
  "changeLog": [
    {
      "version": 8,
      "comment": "HUMAN MEANINGS (contract v1.2.1). Every surface `meaning` is regenerated as the phrase a person would use — section names come from each section's own eyebrow, collections read as “service 2”/“timeline entry 3”, and label surfaces quote the words they currently carry. No surface, pointer, operation or bound changes: this is the text the owner reads in the chat proposal and on the review page."
    },
    {
      "version": 7,
      "comment": "PROSE + LABEL SURFACES (contract v1.2). `site_text_patch` gains 6 prose surfaces (each section's markdown body, written whole below a byte-preserved frontmatter, 8 KiB, prose-only markdown) and 6 label surfaces (primary navigation and hero call-to-action words; `href` stays structural). Primary navigation moved from a component constant into src/data/site.yaml#/nav so it is governed like every other copy string. maxTotalValueBytes raised to 32 KiB so one candidate can carry a body rewrite with its heading. No new operation, artifact class or ceremony: the same site_text_patch review shows every body before/after in full."
    },
    {
      "version": 6,
      "comment": "TEXT SURFACES (contract v1.1). Adds `site_text_patch` over the two governed data files: src/data/site.yaml (homepage hero, doorways, contact intro, jurisdiction note, embassy referral copy, chapter and insights headings, footer identity) and src/data/sections.yaml (every section's eyebrow, title, lede, timeline entries, statistics, service cards and the consul profile). 98 enumerated single-line surfaces; no patterned page records (`patternedSurfaces: null`). Hrefs, CTA labels, icons, the phone and email rows and the Wellington embassy contact facts stay outside the text grammar. Markdown section bodies remain human-owned."
    },
    {
      "version": 6,
      "comment": "WRITABLE VERSION 1 (registration-only contract retired). The consulate's public phone and public email are now single governed facts in src/data/site.yaml, rendered from that one record by the contact section, the footer and the JSON-LD (src/lib/content.ts). This contract declares exactly TWO operations: the closed public_phone_patch coupled set (two pointers, one file) and the schema-v6 public_email_patch (two pointers, one file). It declares NO text-surface, link, typed-page, opening-hours or article operation: section copy lives in markdown frontmatter the text-patch grammar cannot address, navigation is same-page anchors rather than published routes, the site has no typed-page renderer, publishes no opening-hours fact, and its insights are media-bearing PDFs. Each is documented below as denied with its reason, so a proposal for any of them is refused before anything durable exists."
    }
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "src/data/site.yaml",
      "fields": [
        {
          "proposalField": "public_phone",
          "operationKind": "public_phone_patch",
          "inputs": [
            "display",
            "e164"
          ],
          "targets": [
            {
              "jsonPointer": "/contact/rows/0/value",
              "input": "display",
              "render": "raw",
              "matchLiteral": "+64 21 021 68888"
            },
            {
              "jsonPointer": "/contact/rows/0/href",
              "input": "e164",
              "render": "tel",
              "matchLiteral": "tel:+642102168888"
            }
          ],
          "writeMode": "atomic",
          "comment": "The consulate mobile number: one visible display value and one dialable href, both in the Mobile contact row. The contact section, the footer and the JSON-LD `telephone` all render from these two pointers, so this pair IS the complete render-reachable occurrence set. `render: tel` writes the literal `tel:` plus the bare E.164 input; `render: raw` writes the display input verbatim. The Wellington embassy number is a different fact and is not part of this operation."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "preconditions": [
    {
      "comment": "The two governed pointers address contact rows by index, so a reorder of `contact.rows` would silently retarget the phone policy at the email or location row. Before applying any patch, the publisher MUST assert every pointer/value pair below against the BASE revision and refuse the candidate on any mismatch.",
      "path": "src/data/site.yaml",
      "assertions": [
        {
          "jsonPointer": "/contact/rows/0/label",
          "equals": "Mobile"
        },
        {
          "jsonPointer": "/contact/rows/1/label",
          "equals": "Email"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "comment": "CLOSED-SET PRECONDITION. Before applying any public_phone_patch the publisher MUST scan EVERY file under the repository root, excluding only the exact paths in `scanExclusions`, for both literals in RAW TEXT, and every occurrence found MUST be accounted for as a declared target (counted in `expectedOccurrences`) or an explicitly declared `nonRenderingOccurrences` entry. An occurrence that is neither refuses the whole candidate: fewer occurrences means a declared target no longer exists (stale policy, must not write blind); more means an undeclared occurrence appeared in the rendered surface. This site keeps the number in exactly one data record, so there are no non-rendering occurrences to declare.",
      "kind": "closed_set_occurrence_scan",
      "expectedOccurrences": [
        {
          "literal": "+64 21 021 68888",
          "count": 1,
          "comment": "The display form: /contact/rows/0/value."
        },
        {
          "literal": "tel:+642102168888",
          "count": 1,
          "comment": "The dialable href: /contact/rows/0/href."
        }
      ],
      "totalDeclaredTargets": 2,
      "nonRenderingOccurrences": [],
      "nonRenderingOccurrenceRule": "must_be_comment_line",
      "scanExclusions": [
        {
          "path": "node_modules",
          "reason": "Third-party dependencies, never a renderer-owned public fact source."
        },
        {
          "path": ".git",
          "reason": "Historical version-control objects legitimately retain prior values."
        },
        {
          "path": "dist",
          "reason": "Derived build output; governed source bytes are scanned instead."
        },
        {
          "path": ".astro",
          "reason": "Derived Astro cache."
        },
        {
          "path": ".netlify",
          "reason": "Legacy hosting cache; never a source."
        },
        {
          "path": "governance",
          "reason": "Authority documents may quote governed values but do not render."
        },
        {
          "path": "tests",
          "reason": "Regression fixtures do not render."
        },
        {
          "path": "docs",
          "reason": "Project briefs and notes do not render."
        },
        {
          "path": "README.md",
          "reason": "Repository documentation does not render."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "inputContracts": {
    "public_phone": {
      "comment": "CLOSED, TWO-INPUT CONTRACT. A public_phone_patch proposal supplies exactly `display` and `e164` and nothing else; neither has a default and neither may be derived from the other. The `coupledSet` binds both pointers into one atomic write.",
      "inputs": {
        "display": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1,
          "maxLength": 64,
          "comment": "The visible grouping the consulate publishes, written verbatim."
        },
        "e164": {
          "type": "string",
          "pattern": "^\\+[1-9][0-9]{6,14}$",
          "comment": "Bare E.164 digits; the materialiser prefixes `tel:` itself."
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "documentedOperations": [
